### The stories: title and summary (shown in the game menu). The title
### and summary of each chapter are in the file of its story.

histoire-effaceur = The Eraser
    .resume = A creature is erasing everything in the kingdom. Moving around, creating, searching, permissions and sudo, then backups.
histoire-datacenter = The Data Centre
    .resume = A site down, a new recruit, a night of reboots, a fire, an expired certificate: logs, pipes |, accounts and groups, systemd, apt, nginx, backups, TLS.
histoire-paquet = The Lost Packet
    .resume = "The internet doesn't work any more": an investigation, hop by hop, with ping, dig, traceroute and curl.
histoire-temps = The Time Machine
    .resume = Inès's manuscript is damaged: travel through its versions with git.
histoire-archives = The Archives
    .resume = Save a library's collection onto a small USB stick, then find the right version of a manuscript: du, df, find, tar, restic.
histoire-lettres = The Neighbourhood Letters
    .resume = A brand-new server, already under attack: harden SSH, the firewall, fail2ban; then host two sites, DNS, survive the night of the concert, move SSH without locking yourself out, and hunt down repeat offenders.
histoire-fabrique = The Workshop
    .resume = The neighbourhood fablab moves to containers: docker, volumes, docker compose, the firewall Docker bypasses, and containers that no longer run as root.
histoire-gazette = The Gazette
    .resume = The neighbourhood's online newspaper learns to deploy: git push, hooks, and rolling back when things break.
histoire-ludotheque = The Game Library
    .resume = The server of the neighbourhood game library: ransomware, backups that hold up, and a database to rescue properly.
histoire-astreinte = On Call
    .resume = Nights on call for Radio Quartier: full disk, memory, inodes, clock… then monitoring that warns you before things break, and the disk that saturates every afternoon.
histoire-maison = The Community Centre
    .resume = A gateway and an internal network behind it: your own SSH keys, ssh -J, tunnels, scp and rsync between machines.
histoire-cooperative = The Co-op
    .resume = The neighbourhood food co-op: accounts for the people who arrive and leave, shared permissions, a well-tuned sudo, the till's website and its updates, by hand and then automatic.
histoire-ruche = The Hive
    .resume = The network of a community space: VLANs to separate offices, guests and equipment, DHCP, NAT and a firewall between zones, a VPN, a DMZ for the website, a second site, a directory and enterprise Wi-Fi.
histoire-audit = The Audit
    .resume = The bakery's insurer wants an audit: fix an auditor's findings (SSH, accounts, sudo, secrets), close what is exposed on the network, then trace a login nobody expected.
